guide forever/collectibles/mounts/horde/paladin-warhorse
title Paladin Warhorse (Forsaken)
category Class
folder Paladin
keywords Summon Warhorse, Report to Danitha, A Paladin's Steed, Garen Largo, Danitha Morr, Bandarion Keep, Apprentice Riding, Forsaken Paladin, Paladin, class mount
reward spell 1279399 "Summon Warhorse"
why Your first mount at 40, summoned at will: a Forsaken paladin buys no horse and pays no riding trainer.
faction Horde
race Undead
class Paladin
levels 40-60
zone Undercity

# Summon Warhorse for Forsaken paladins, new in Forever (#2898, asked for by
# Blitz): Report to Danitha (97022) from Garen Largo, the paladin trainer in
# the Undercity, then A Paladin's Steed (94971) from Danitha Morr at Bandarion
# Keep, accepted and handed straight back to her: the hand-in teaches the
# mount. Both quests are level 40, Undead Paladins only, and ask for nothing.
# Sources: players' recordings to 2026-11-18 (builds 70862 to 70938): Garen
# Largo offered Report to Danitha at 40 to 5 people, who all handed it in to
# Danitha Morr and took A Paladin's Steed from her window; 6 people handed A
# Paladin's Steed in to her, and at each hand-in the game taught Apprentice
# Riding (33388) and set Riding to 75 at once. One of them later summoned the
# Forsaken Summon Warhorse (spell 1279399). Forever's client tables
# (1.60.1.70888): the quest's teaching spell 1279400 teaches Summon Warhorse
# 1279399 (Mount 2923) and Apprentice Riding 33388. Forever's quest data
# (QuestieDB's Forever rows) for givers, enders, levels and the Undead Paladin
# masks.
# Report to Danitha is a lead-in, not a prerequisite: one player who never
# had it was offered A Paladin's Steed by Danitha at 40 after training at the
# keep, and QuestieDB's Forever data gives A Paladin's Steed no prerequisite
# (forever-db/corrections/quests.json, 94971 and 97022). The guide takes it
# anyway: it pays XP, and the Undercity's trainer is where most Forsaken
# paladins train at 40.
# The level 60 Forsaken Charger chain (A Worthy Endeavor 97174 and on) is not
# here: Forever's data has no givers or steps for most of it and no recording
# shows it yet.

step Report to Danitha
  tip At 40 Garen Largo, the paladin trainer in the Undercity, sends you to Danitha Morr at Bandarion Keep. Train your new spells with him while you are there. Already at Bandarion Keep? Skip this step: Danitha gives you the mount quest without it.
  level 40
  accept 97022 npc 260093             -- Garen Largo
  train 260093 optional               -- Garen Largo: your level 40 spells

step Danitha Morr
  zone Tirisfal Glades
  when onquest 97022
  tip Bandarion Keep stands on the bluffs in western Tirisfal, north-west of the Solliden Farmstead: leave the Undercity and follow the road west past Brill. Danitha Morr is inside the keep, upstairs.
  turnin 97022                        -- Danitha Morr

step Summon Warhorse
  zone Tirisfal Glades
  tip Danitha Morr, upstairs in Bandarion Keep, offers A Paladin's Steed at 40: accept it and hand it straight back. It teaches you Summon Warhorse and Apprentice Riding together, so you need no horse and no riding trainer.
  level 40
  accept 94971                        -- Danitha Morr
  turnin 94971                        -- Danitha Morr: Summon Warhorse
